  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">template &lt;typename... Args&gt; [[noreturn]] void Abort (const Args &amp;...                  args) noexcept;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Abort the current operation This function will never return to its caller. The stack is not unwound: destructors of variables with automatic storage duration are not called. Calling this function is ill-formed if any of the arguments is not convertible to <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"ns_core_ara_core_e30e31.html\">ara::core</a>:: StringView.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
